     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Leaflet.Draw has a nice way of drawing polygon&#39;s interactively. I would like to be able to access this (or some other way to interactively draw a polygon on a map) from within a Shiny app and to retrieve the coordinates.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Extensive search has, surprisingly, not uncovered anything. </p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">I would like to find an existing R package that allows for the drawing of polygons in a similar way that markers can be set as editable, I would like to be able to create edit polygons directly on the map. </p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Is anyone working on a port of Leaflet.Draw or some other way to edit polygons?</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Thanks</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,36,38);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p></div>"
